@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] complete-before-forward
In enforcing modes, inference forwarding MUST wait for complete inspection of all
discovered supported content. Unsupported attachments and incomplete inspection
MUST cause rejection, not an uninspected pass-through.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] diagnostics-no-content
Runtime logs and Preflight-generated client errors MUST NOT contain request bodies, extracted text,
matched secrets, authorization values, worker stderr, or original filenames.
Opaque upstream response bodies are forwarded as part of API compatibility.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] cache-not-authority
Only complete inspection results MAY enter the approval cache. Cache failures
MUST NOT authorize forwarding. Cache identity MUST include exact content bytes,
security scope, and all behavior-affecting inspection configuration.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:testing] pure-core-properties
New pure scanner, document, cache-generation, and policy behavior MUST have Hegel
properties in addition to exact regression fixtures where appropriate.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] static-types-required
All handwritten and generated programming-language source MUST use static types.
Project-owned executables, workers, and update utilities MUST be Rust. Compiler
and clippy checks MUST cover all Rust targets and test features. NixOS options
MUST pass module evaluation and the NixOS test driver's type checks.
